{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01FfxBBGVHKogkrBSqCubznU","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tname: implement-change\n3\tdescription: Use when you take a task (bug fix, feature, refactor) in taiga-back and need to go from the request to a verified change ready for a pull request.\n4\t---\n5\t\n6\t# Implement a change in taiga-back\n7\t\n8\t1. Prepare the environment once per clone:\n9\t   ```bash\n10\t   make setup\n11\t   ```\n12\t   It creates `.venv` (Python 3.10), installs the requirements, installs the pre-push hook and starts PostgreSQL from `compose.yaml`. Details and common problems: `docs/local-dev.md`.\n13\t\n14\t2. Find the code. API routes are in `taiga/routers.py`; each domain app has `api.py`, `models.py`, `services.py`, `serializers.py`, `validators.py`, `permissions.py`. Read `docs/architecture.md` for the map and `docs/product.md` for domain terms (milestone = sprint, US = user story, OCC).\n15\t\n16\t3. Write the test first when you fix a bug. Unit tests live in `tests/unit`, API tests in `tests/integration`, permission matrices in `tests/integration/resources_permissions`. Build data with `tests/factories.py` (`from tests import factories as f`). Run only your test:\n17\t   ```bash\n18\t   .venv/bin/pytest tests/integration/test_userstories.py -k <name> --reuse-db\n19\t   ```\n20\t   Confirm it fails for the right reason.\n21\t\n22\t4. Make the change. Rules:\n23\t   - Use `taiga.base.api` viewsets and `taiga.base.exceptions` (for example `exc.BadRequest`), not Django REST framework.\n24\t   - Wrap user-facing strings in `gettext` (`_()`); do not edit `taiga/locale/*.po` (Weblate manages them).\n25\t   - Keep the MPL license header at the top of new Python files (copy it from a neighbour file).\n26\t   - Async work must also run when `CELERY_ENABLED` is false (see `docs/decisions/0002-celery-with-rabbitmq-and-pickle.md`).\n27\t\n28\t5. If you changed a model, create the migration and check it:\n29\t   ```bash\n30\t   DJANGO_SETTINGS_MODULE=tests.config .venv/bin/python manage.py makemigrations <app_label>\n31\t   make migrations-check\n32\t   ```\n33\t\n34\t6. Run the fast gate. It must pass before you say the change is done:\n35\t   ```bash\n36\t   make check-fast\n37\t   ```\n38\t   For changes outside `tests/unit` coverage (API, permissions, signals), also run the related integration files, or `make check` (whole suite, slow).\n39\t\n40\t7. Optional style check on the files you touched (the gate only enforces syntax rules, old code has many violations):\n41\t   ```bash\n42\t   .venv/bin/flake8 path/to/changed_file.py\n43\t   ```\n44\t\n45\t8. Commit with a conventional commit message (`fix: ...`, `feat: ...`, `test: ...`), on a branch, never on `main`. Add an entry to `docs/harness/log.md` if the change is significant (date, what changed, what you learned, what is left).\n46\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"89e56f5e-87d6-46d3-b8ae-5b8e80d3a044","uuid":"a6a26b06-66a6-40a9-8c7b-e5a25a362199","timestamp":"2026-11-01T14:51:28.316Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/victor/Repos/unwritten/uw-harness-cases/taiga/repo/.agents/skills/implement-change/SKILL.md","content":"---\nname: implement-change\ndescription: Use when you take a task (bug fix, feature, refactor) in taiga-back and need to go from the request to a verified change ready for a pull request.\n---\n\n# Implement a change in taiga-back\n\n1. Prepare the environment once per clone:\n   ```bash\n   make setup\n   ```\n   It creates `.venv` (Python 3.10), installs the requirements, installs the pre-push hook and starts PostgreSQL from `compose.yaml`. Details and common problems: `docs/local-dev.md`.\n\n2. Find the code. API routes are in `taiga/routers.py`; each domain app has `api.py`, `models.py`, `services.py`, `serializers.py`, `validators.py`, `permissions.py`. Read `docs/architecture.md` for the map and `docs/product.md` for domain terms (milestone = sprint, US = user story, OCC).\n\n3. Write the test first when you fix a bug. Unit tests live in `tests/unit`, API tests in `tests/integration`, permission matrices in `tests/integration/resources_permissions`. Build data with `tests/factories.py` (`from tests import factories as f`). Run only your test:\n   ```bash\n   .venv/bin/pytest tests/integration/test_userstories.py -k <name> --reuse-db\n   ```\n   Confirm it fails for the right reason.\n\n4. Make the change. Rules:\n   - Use `taiga.base.api` viewsets and `taiga.base.exceptions` (for example `exc.BadRequest`), not Django REST framework.\n   - Wrap user-facing strings in `gettext` (`_()`); do not edit `taiga/locale/*.po` (Weblate manages them).\n   - Keep the MPL license header at the top of new Python files (copy it from a neighbour file).\n   - Async work must also run when `CELERY_ENABLED` is false (see `docs/decisions/0002-celery-with-rabbitmq-and-pickle.md`).\n\n5. If you changed a model, create the migration and check it:\n   ```bash\n   DJANGO_SETTINGS_MODULE=tests.config .venv/bin/python manage.py makemigrations <app_label>\n   make migrations-check\n   ```\n\n6. Run the fast gate. It must pass before you say the change is done:\n   ```bash\n   make check-fast\n   ```\n   For changes outside `tests/unit` coverage (API, permissions, signals), also run the related integration files, or `make check` (whole suite, slow).\n\n7. Optional style check on the files you touched (the gate only enforces syntax rules, old code has many violations):\n   ```bash\n   .venv/bin/flake8 path/to/changed_file.py\n   ```\n\n8. Commit with a conventional commit message (`fix: ...`, `feat: ...`, `test: ...`), on a branch, never on `main`. Add an entry to `docs/harness/log.md` if the change is significant (date, what changed, what you learned, what is left).\n","numLines":46,"startLine":1,"totalLines":46}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01FfxBBGVHKogkrBSqCubznU","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
